+# The Board (ext-board.js)
+
+One sheet with four cards: **Plan my day**, the **Week board**, the **Habit heatmap** and **Pomodoro stats**. Open it with the
+**Board** button on Today, "The Board" in All tools, the palette ("Board", "Plan my day", "Habit heatmap", "Pomodoro stats"), or the
+links `#board`, `#plan-my-day`, `#week-board`, `#habit-heatmap`, `#focus-stats`.
+
+- **Plan my day** reads today's free gaps, your open tasks (today and overdue) and the bots' trading window: entries 02:00-15:30 ET,
+  the NY open 09:30 ET, flat 15:55 ET, weekdays only (converted to your clock by the Planner's own ET converter). It proposes where each
+  task fits and why: overdue first, big or high-priority tasks in a quiet stretch (after the bots are flat, or before the open), short
+  ones in short gaps, a 15-minute pre-open prep slot and a 20-minute journal slot after flat. Tasks that fit no gap are listed. It also
+  reads the bots' last live status (`planner.ext.live`, the copy Bots and projects keeps; read only) and adds a line when a bot is in
+  a trade, looks stopped, or the eval room is thin. Nothing is written: Copy puts the plan on the clipboard.
+- **Week board**: Monday to Sunday (swipe sideways, arrows for other weeks). Each day: its events, its tasks, and a load bar (open task
+  minutes against 60% of the free time, red when over). A round tick marks a task done, the arrow moves it to the next day; both go through
+  the Planner's own snapshot / commit, so Undo works.
+- **Habit heatmap**: the last 12 weeks of every habit (Mon-Sun columns), the run you are on, the best run, the share of the last 30 days.
+- **Pomodoro stats**: focus minutes today, this week against the week before, the average day over 14 days, 14 bars, the best day,
+  rounds today and the top projects (from the focus minutes the Focus mode logs on each task).
+
+Code: `planner/ext-board.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-board.js">` in `<head>` after ext-temple.js; it waits for `planner:ready`.
+Storage: none of its own. Pure helpers for the tests: `window.__bd` (`planDay`, `heat`, `pomo`, `planText`, `BOT`). Test: `planner/tests/board.test.js`.
